ll,"open_fixes":0,"blocked_fixes":19,"forecast_issued_utc":"2026-10-20T00:00:00Z","breaks":[]}],"named":[]},"thresholds":{"change_share":0.15,"lead_margin":0.05,"min_span_h":6,"period_ahead_h":12},"text":{"line":"Morning briefing 6:06 AM","entries":[["Overview","Sunrise is at 6:57 AM with 11 h 11 m of daylight. Overnight at North Island, no rain; air 64\u201371 \u00b0F (18\u201322 \u00b0C) and humidity 76\u201390%, 64 \u00b0F (18 \u00b0C) and 90% at 5:52 AM. Water 73 \u00b0F (22.5 \u00b0C) at CDIP 191, 73\u201376 \u00b0F (22.5\u201324.2 \u00b0C) over the night."],["Swell","CDIP 191 at 5:00 AM: 14.3 s from S 183\u00b0, 3.0 ft (0.93 m); 11.1 s from W 271\u00b0, 2.9 ft (0.87 m); wind sea 4.2 s from WNW 298\u00b0, 1.2 ft (0.36 m). At 11:00 AM yesterday: 15.4 s from S 190\u00b0, 4.4 ft (1.33 m); 12.5 s from W 280\u00b0, 3.4 ft (1.05 m). Breaking at 5:00 AM, against 11:00 AM yesterday: North 3.5 ft (1.07 m), little change; Center 3.6 ft (1.09 m), little change; South 3.5 ft (1.05 m), little change. Coming: north-west swell (280\u2013330\u00b0) rose at Tanner Banks (NDBC 46047) from 7:56 PM yesterday, 14\u201317 s first, then 12\u201314 s from 12:05 AM; by deep-water speed it was due at CDIP 191 around 11:31 PM yesterday, at the breaks 30\u201340 min after. Due, not seen."],["Tide","The tide is pushing to 5.9 ft (1.81 m) at 7:13 AM then dropping to 3.3 ft (1.02 m) at 12:57 PM. The previous AM low was 2.0 ft (0.61 m) at 12:40 AM and the PM high will be 6.0 ft (1.84 m) at 6:43 PM. The gauge is running 1.4 ft (0.43 m) over the harmonic prediction, over the last 3 days. Today's range is 3.9 ft (1.20 m), building toward springs; springs around Oct 25. On the 2016 survey the tide moves where the waves break, not how big they are; this season's sandbars are not known."],["Wind","E 90\u00b0 at 3 mph (3 kt) at 5:52 AM: light cross-shore at North; light offshore at Center and South. At this hour on the 30 days before: North light or variable on 12, offshore on 13; Center light or variable on 12; South light or variable on 12, offshore on 13. Median 5 mph (4 kt)."],["Watching","Former hurricane [Trudy](https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/archive/2026/TRUDY_graphics.php): every fix NHC has logged or forecast is behind land from Point Loma South, so nothing it has sent reaches the breaks."]]}}